{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/991204-how-aware-are-solars-of-their-own-charms","id":991204,"title":"How aware are Solars of their own Charms?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-21T18:27:22-07:00","id":991204,"title":"How aware are Solars of their own Charms?","content":"I'll open with an example here: Player 1 purchases Soul-Light Spreading Discipline (apologies for those who haven't read Miracles of the Solar Exalted yet!) for their character because their character concept is of a charismatic but reluctant leader, who tries to dissuade people from worshipping him, but only ends up convincing his followers that their messiah is truly humble and wise.<br /> <br /> Player 2 makes the argument that Player 1's Solar cannot possess such a charm unconsciously, but rather that by purchasing that charm, it means that Solar 1 must desire to be worshipped and is open to moral judgement for possessing this charm by Solar 2.<br /> <br /> I was under the impression after reading the 3E charm section that a Solar's charms are not necessarily explicit techniques that they actively acquire through training and effort, but are (or at least can be) abilities that they manifest just by being *that awesome* or as abilities granted by their patron at the moment of Exaltation (leading to possible &quot;I did not ask for this, dad!&quot; scenarios), or even a combination of the three.<br /> <br /> Can a Solar possess abilities that they didn't consciously or unconsciously ask for? Am I completely wrong? Do you think it's more complicated?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12339,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12339-liberty-king-gandalf","user":"Liberty King Gandalf","date":". 10-21-2016, 09:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12339-liberty-king-gandalf","name":"Liberty King Gandalf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T18:36:46-07:00","id":991207,"title":"","content":"I would put it somewhere in the middle. An exalt can develop and use charms subconsciously, but they do not develop charms that act against their will. They can develop charms they did not ask for. They just cannot develop charms that they do not want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12550-oglantash","name":"OGLantash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T20:01:29-07:00","id":991232,"title":"","content":"My call on this is that Solar abilities are an expression of their own talents. They are aware of their talents and the ways in which their gifts can be applied. <br /> <br /> Normally, I'd say that a charm cannot produce effects its user would not want. However, it's not unreasonable for an uncannily persuasive person to wind up persuading people of things they never intended. I would err on the side of whatever you think makes the better story in this case. <br /> <br /> Obligatory Monty Python Clip:<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QereR0CViMY\" data-code=\"QereR0CViMY\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/QereR0CViMY/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T20:30:53-07:00","id":991239,"title":"","content":"This is pretty much exactly what the introduction to the Charms chapter is supposed to address. So yes, your third paragraph is correct.<br /> <br /> I would definitely allow a Solar to have and use a Charm subconsciously. Especially something like Soul-Light Spreading Discipline, which I envision as being ... like the Buddha, I suppose. He isn't exactly worshipped directly. People follow his teachings and try to emulate him to become enlightened themselves.<br /> <br /> So no, I definitely wouldn't say Soul-Light Spreading Discipline is something that a character should be aware of or that should be used to judge the character that has it. Especially in the animist, theistic world of Exalted, where you can get people to deify you completely by accident. I wouldn't even say that any character involved is necessarily aware of what's happening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3353-rca","name":"RCa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T20:52:36-07:00","id":991254,"title":"","content":"Agreed, per the rules as written charms should be able to be developed and used unconsciously. Somewhat relevantly in my current campaign my Eclipse activated Harmonious Presence Meditation at the moment of Exaltation with the indefinite version. In play and my headcannon she isn't even aware its going on and doesn't know how to turn it off at all. Its just always going.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12429-viragos","name":"Viragos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T21:31:01-07:00","id":991269,"title":"","content":"I would say there is no way a Solar can use a charm and not know it. The disconnect here is that the developers were trying to impress upon readers that charms are an extension of the Solar's power. Not like a Martial Art Technique to be learned, or a sorcerous working/spell that must be coaxed from the world. Solar's charms are a perfect extension of the Solar's will, their essence, effort, and their breath. Essence fever urges them to go beyond human, to push into the supernatural, the essence rushes through their minds, bodies, and exaltations. Every single time they use a charm the fever is felt. I don't think it's possible for one of the exalted could use a charm without knowing they are influencing the world in some way, that isn't to say they couldn't subconsciously use a charm but once it rushes to the surface they know it happened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ex3 Craft <a href=\"http://madletter.net/rpg/exalted/maudova/Craft_Rewrite.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">rewrite</a>.<br /> ExEssence <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18jTwAx0Pldsg5Zt-63HW77zprWvXRTsmz4VrRKZvB8c/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Community Homebrew Compilation</a><br /> Twitter Handle: at maudovajr<br /> Discord Handle: Maudova","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12102-maudova","name":"Maudova","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T21:52:24-07:00","id":991274,"title":"","content":"At my table it would be fine. Enabling the story of the reluctant leader who gathers worshipers without meaning to do it is more important than the technicalities of if Charms were intended to be that way or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T22:26:38-07:00","id":991284,"title":"","content":"I'd point out to Player 2 that<br /> <br /> 1) following the Solar's teachings mechanically functions like belonging to a Cult, but without necessarily being worship of the Solar, so while the Solar draws power from people following her teachings and passing them on, this is not strictly speaking direct worship - the students and 'grandstudents' may not even be aware of the link between teachings and granting the Solar power, and would laugh at the idea of 'rotate crops like so, be kind to others, and help your fellow people' being called &quot;worship&quot;.<br /> <br /> and 2) There's no such thing as 'justification for moralization' in any sort of 'word from on high' in Exalted. If you feel people doing something is wrong by all means correct them, moralize at them, teach them what you believe to be right, but there's no Yahweh saying Thou Shalt Worship None But I that makes anything vaguely cult-like flat-out Bad-Wrong, for the particular example. Things might have bad intentions, like a cult that tortures people into following its' strictures, or bad outcomes, like a cult going mad, drinking koolaid, and mass-suiciding because of some twisted belief structure, but there's no D&amp;D-style &quot;capital-E reads to Divine Alignment spells as Evil&quot; to it that is objectively true.<br /> <br /> As far as the possibility of the people who follow your teachings in turn becoming direct worshippers praying fervently to your greatness, I'd leave that possibility up between ST and GM. Two characters with these charms might both intend to pass on teachings and not be actually directly worshipped, and if one's player wanted to actually inspire worship as well in spite of the character's wishes, I'd be okay with it [though I'd not give them &quot;doubled cult&quot; for it, just IC responses of people thanking the Holy Teacher and acting in a manner befitting divinity, while the other guy has people eagerly listening to his words and writing them down to pass them on without the trappings of worship].<br /> <br /> And as far as the general concept of Charm Awareness, I would say that Solars should be considered aware of the idea of active charms, IE: simple, supplemental, reflexive, but not in the sense of &quot;If I use Heaven Thunder Hammer, I can send someone flying three range bands&quot;, but rather &quot;If I put my all into a single blow, I can send my enemy flying!&quot;. For the Lore charms, it would be &quot;People take readily to my teachings as a holistic whole, both practical applications and philosophical tenets, when I pass on ideas and training&quot;, rather than &quot;If I instruct people in adequately expensive improvements to their abilities I can force Defining intimacies upon them&quot;.<br /> <br /> Permanent charms, I think are something they might notice, but most easily attribute to simply being 'that good', or happen to forget about when narratively or personally convenient. &quot;My skill as a teacher empowers me in turn when my tenets are followed&quot; rather than &quot;The more I shove lessons down people's throats, the more I can exploit this charm to draw cult power&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","user":"Meianno Yuurei","date":". 10-22-2016, 01:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T22:49:48-07:00","id":991291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Liberty King Gandalf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/991204-how-aware-are-solars-of-their-own-charms#post991204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll open with an example here: Player 1 purchases Soul-Light Spreading Discipline (apologies for those who haven't read Miracles of the Solar Exalted yet!) for their character because their character concept is of a charismatic but reluctant leader, who tries to dissuade people from worshipping him, but only ends up convincing his followers that their messiah is truly humble and wise.<br /> <br /> Player 2 makes the argument that Player 1's Solar cannot possess such a charm unconsciously, but rather that by purchasing that charm, it means that Solar 1 must desire to be worshipped and is open to moral judgement for possessing this charm by Solar 2.<br /> <br /> I was under the impression after reading the 3E charm section that a Solar's charms are not necessarily explicit techniques that they actively acquire through training and effort, but are (or at least can be) abilities that they manifest just by being *that awesome* or as abilities granted by their patron at the moment of Exaltation (leading to possible &quot;I did not ask for this, dad!&quot; scenarios), or even a combination of the three.<br /> <br /> Can a Solar possess abilities that they didn't consciously or unconsciously ask for? Am I completely wrong? Do you think it's more complicated?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that the way it usually happens is that the character is either actively or passively using essence, much in the same way the various element Benders from Avatar are actively and intentionally moving chi around when they manipulate the elements.<br /> <br /> That said, there are some charms which represent passive benefits or even active things that the character can't have real control over. The various surprise negation charms, for example, can't be directly activated by a surprised character, because they wouldn't know they were being attacked. They're activated by the player.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, all charms are activated by the player, regardless of the character's wants and desires. As such, if the player wants to represent a character who is just such an awesome speaker, that everyone loves him, regardless of his feelings about it, then I think that is a legit way of playing the character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=N_oQkSh2lq8\" data-code=\"N_oQkSh2lq8\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/N_oQkSh2lq8/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T22:55:51-07:00","id":991292,"title":"","content":"My understanding is as follows:<br /> <br /> First, it's important to remember that you can't actually use a Charm until you've purchased it, something that takes both time (Ability in days) and experience points. In the middle of battle a player can't just suddenly say, &quot;My character uses Shadow Replacement Technique,&quot; if their character hasn't spent the experience points and 5 days of time training to use Shadow Replacement Technique.<br /> <br /> So you can't &quot;accidentally&quot; learn and use a Charm, since you actually have to spend several days training with that Charm to learn and memorize how to properly move the Essence through your body.<br /> <br /> A Solar might have 5 dots of Melee, but he can't simply channel his Essence in conjunction with his sword swings without some training and learning how to do that first (ie - purchasing Melee Charms). A Solar that has not spent time training to channel his Essence in conjunction with melee attacks (that is, a Solar with no Melee Charms) can't really use or channel Essence with his melee attacks.<br /> <br /> The other thing to keep in mind is that natural (splat) Charms aren't really a thing in game - in character, the Solar who is using the Melee Excellency and Hungry Tiger Technique is just simply channeling Essence through his sword arm while he's attacking. But, before he <i>could</i> channel Essence through his sword arm, he would first have to spend time (and experience points) training his body and soul in how to do that.<br /> <br /> Individual ST's, of course, are free to waive training times and such, allowing players to subconsciously learn Charms without actually spending time figuring out how to do stuff. Personally, this is what I do in my games because I think it's much more interesting and makes for better drama.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T23:13:38-07:00","id":991298,"title":"","content":"My dream scenario: A Solar dancer give his all to this one performance but doesn't know that being too good in front of a bunch of nobles will make a lot of stuff rise, now has a swarm of horny people wanting him to be their..........eh...........how do you call a male mistress ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T23:41:22-07:00","id":991302,"title":"","content":"&quot;Finally, a word on advancing mystical traits. While it is possible to give instruction in Charms, most Chosen, and certainly most Solars, develop their own Charms through instinctive cultivation of skill rather than through rigorous practice. As such, while Charms can certainly be trained like any other skill, many characters \u2018train\u2019 their Charms by exercising the Ability in question under duress.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T04:25:17-07:00","id":991334,"title":"","content":"Re: OP, your actions having a effect you didn't intend them to, like people deciding that you're a deity against your will because of your actions, is a pretty good Exalted dilemma. Doing acts of essence fueled heroism (Charms) without intending to, I think not really do much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T13:45:31-07:00","id":991513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/991204-how-aware-are-solars-of-their-own-charms?p=991298#post991298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My dream scenario: A Solar dancer give his all to this one performance but doesn't know that being too good in front of a bunch of nobles will make a lot of stuff rise, now has a swarm of horny people wanting him to be their..........eh...........how do you call a male mistress ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lover, paramour, playmate, catamite (if you want to be insulting)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T14:17:06-07:00","id":991528,"title":"","content":"Apart from permanent Charms, I'd say it's impossible for any Exalted to use a Charm without being aware of doing something; every Exalt is always aware of their Essence, of its shifts and flows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T17:52:23-07:00","id":991628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/991204-how-aware-are-solars-of-their-own-charms?p=991298#post991298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My dream scenario: A Solar dancer give his all to this one performance but doesn't know that being too good in front of a bunch of nobles will make a lot of stuff rise, now has a swarm of horny people wanting him to be their..........eh...........how do you call a male mistress ?</div> </div> </div> </div>...Catamite? Except that usually refers to children... Consort?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T19:58:50-07:00","id":991671,"title":"","content":"I would inform player 2 that she should mind her own character sheet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T20:41:20-07:00","id":991692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Liberty King Gandalf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/991204-how-aware-are-solars-of-their-own-charms#post991204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Player 1 purchases Soul-Light Spreading Discipline (apologies for those who haven't read Miracles of the Solar Exalted yet!)...</div> </div> </div> </div>Instead of apologizing, you could just say what it does so everyone is on the same page.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Player 2 makes the argument that Player 1's Solar cannot possess such a charm unconsciously, but rather that by purchasing that charm, it means that Solar 1 must desire to be worshipped and is open to moral judgement for possessing this charm by Solar 2. </div> </div> </div>That's incorrect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can a Solar possess abilities that they didn't consciously or unconsciously ask for? </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T23:08:23-07:00","id":991744,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think the problem is player 2 thinking the setting or rules give any mind to their &quot;moral judgement&quot;.<br /> <br /> If player 2's character thinks something player 1's character is *doing* is wrong, that's one thing. But character 2 judging character 1 because of a Charm that character 1 knows is nonsense on it's face because character 2 can't read characater 1's sheet in any case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T23:36:01-07:00","id":991754,"title":"","content":"The best way I've found to confer this is that Solars are neither Batman or Wizards, but Jedi. So maybe a power like force lightning can be looked at and go &quot;Okay that's a unique skill that's very obvious and discrete.&quot; but a Jedi also has powers like enhanced reflexes and greater stamina, which are absolutely force based and also utterly indistinguishable from their innate strength, except by magnitude.<br /> <br /> So in this case I really think that this charm is more a case of the latter. Player 2 has as much right to judge Player 1 for taking that charm as a pod-racer does for calling Anakin Skywalker a cheater for using his force enhanced reflexes to compete. It's not like he can just consciously turn it off and sever his connection to the luminous heartbeat of the universe!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T01:58:57-07:00","id":991771,"title":"","content":"Player 1: &quot;Hey, I really like this Charm, but I'd like its effects to subvert my character's intentions. Is that a thing I can do?&quot;<br /> ST: &quot;So you're like the God-Emperor, becoming the focus of worship despite your best efforts? I can dig it. If you want to pay the XP, go for it.&quot;<br /> Player 2: &quot;But that's not how Charms work! They're effects of superlative skill and directed will!&quot;<br /> ST: &quot;You're right. That is how Solar Charms work... normally. In this case, it's more of a mechanical description of an unintended consequence, and I'm allowing it.&quot;<br /> <br /> I find this especially plausible because it's a Permanent Charm that you don't have to invest any Essence in. It's just an added effect to what you were already doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T02:17:38-07:00","id":991774,"title":"","content":"I agree, I see no issue with it. It doesn't require any effort on their part, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T02:41:43-07:00","id":991783,"title":"","content":"I would like to say that being aware of your essence doesn't mean you are aware of specific charms. From the moment of exaltation, you are filled with essence and you may or may not be aware of exactly what that means. In sports, sometimes you are just better than you thought you could be. Your muscles move just right, your breath goes at the perfect pace and your intentions work out perfectly. Basically the stars align because you try hard. I imagine that's what essence feels like only grander. An exalt would most likely be aware that he is channeling his essence into what he is doing <u>if the is paying attention</u>. However, the presence of essence has become as constant as breathing and how many people pay attention to that. <br /> <br /> I very much doubt there is a distinct difference between pumping essence into an excellency and using excellent strike unless the exalt actively tries to find that difference. To him, he is simply fighting, trying to find an opening and making unconcious decisions about how to flex which muscle. I always found my best results in sports came about when I was not focusing on what I was doing and simply did.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, from a gameplay point of view, playing a Jessica Jones-esque Killgrave is much more interessting than playing yet another mind_dominator_03. I think player 2 needs to take a step and look at the big picture of what makes the game fun for each individual rather than insisting that mechanics work a certain way. Character's aren't aware of the difference between withering and decisive atttacks either and the world works just fine without that mechanical distinction. It's an integral part of the gameplay but it has zero bearing on the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10990-beaumis","name":"Beaumis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10990_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T06:38:33-07:00","id":991824,"title":"","content":"I agree with Ren9077 on this one. It is a Permanent effect, so it doesn't require conscious effort to apply. The character's desire to spread knowledge changed his Essence and now his teachings are doctrines, dogmas, scripture and prophecy to some.<br /> <br /> For active use Charms, I would say no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T06:51:14-07:00","id":991832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/991204-how-aware-are-solars-of-their-own-charms?p=991671#post991671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would inform player 2 that she should mind her own character sheet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this should be a last ditch kind of response, if it is ever given, as it is just hostile and dismissive.<br /> <br /> If a player is sufficiently involved in the setting/game to care about how Essence and Charms and agency interact, I think some time and effort should be dispensed on the issue. Note that I'm not saying there has to be thesis defense here. Or even that everyone has to be satisfied by the outcome. Just the courtesy of hearing and addressing someone's ideas or concerns.<br /> <br /> The world is built by all players (ST is a player) together, telling people outright to only mind their character is counter productive to world building.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T11:09:28-07:00","id":991915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/991204-how-aware-are-solars-of-their-own-charms?p=991832#post991832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The world is built by all players (ST is a player) together, telling people outright to only mind their character is counter productive to world building.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is important to remember. Whenever a GM decides to change a rule, or a player has a poor understanding of an existing rule, it's better for the GM to carefully explain why she has chosen to interpret the rule in the way she did rather than simply dismiss the player's complaint. It's vital that everyone understands what is happening with the rules in the game they are playing and why the GM is making the judgements that she is making.<br /> <br /> Few things can hurt enjoyment of a game more than feeling that the GM is playing fast and loose with the rules in favor of another player while dismissing your own objections out of hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T12:53:36-07:00","id":991966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/991204-how-aware-are-solars-of-their-own-charms?p=991832#post991832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this should be a last ditch kind of response, if it is ever given, as it is just hostile and dismissive.<br /> <br /> If a player is sufficiently involved in the setting/game to care about how Essence and Charms and agency interact, I think some time and effort should be dispensed on the issue. Note that I'm not saying there has to be thesis defense here. Or even that everyone has to be satisfied by the outcome. Just the courtesy of hearing and addressing someone's ideas or concerns.<br /> <br /> The world is built by all players (ST is a player) together, telling people outright to only mind their character is counter productive to world building.</div> </div> </div> </div>Consciously choosing to have one's character plan to judge and nitpick another player's character for having a Charm from a published book is a good way to be counter-productive to that second player's <i>enjoyment of the game</i>, worldbuilding be damned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:courier\">REALITY.SYS corrupt. Reboot Universe? Y/N/Q</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/230-taichara","name":"taichara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar230_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T13:22:51-07:00","id":991983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>taichara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/991204-how-aware-are-solars-of-their-own-charms?p=991966#post991966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Consciously choosing to have one's character plan to judge and nitpick another player's character for having a Charm from a published book is a good way to be counter-productive to that second player's <i>enjoyment of the game</i>, worldbuilding be damned.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, maybe that player is reacting that way because they THOUGHT they had a good idea of concepts, but that idea is now being subverted. Explain to them that they've got the right general idea, but in this specific case, you're using the rules to represent something subtly different. Also, that they're welcome to put their own creative spin on the rules this way. Assuming everyone's operating in good faith has a way of keeping things calm and civil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T13:52:07-07:00","id":991995,"title":"","content":"@Jen, toyboy is the closest specific word I can think of that sort of implies a male mistress (... but it only applies when your fancy piece is a bit younger, so may be a bit out if you're thinking about sexy &quot;Uncles&quot; ).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2746_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2746\" data-vbnamecard=\"2746\">TGUEIROS</a>, if a Charm says in the Charm it doesn't take conscious effect to apply and has forever changed his essence and such, I'd go with that. Otherwise I would be a bit leery about just deducing that from the rules. (Insert here standard Rules Are Not Physics and Charms Are Abstractions boilerplate we're all already bored of. We all know the drill.).<br /> <br /> Being permanent and having no cost could just be because the writers thought it wasn't worth making players track the cost of it or run out of essence for it, rather than because it literally isn't something that the character chooses to exert effort and control to do. Mind, you could certainly go either way if there's nothing specific.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T14:38:20-07:00","id":992019,"title":"","content":"As far as I'm concerned, it's impossible for any Exalt not to be aware of using a Charm with an Essence cost. It is possible to use a Charm with no Essence cost without being aware of it, if the Charm has no other costs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T14:47:44-07:00","id":992029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/991204-how-aware-are-solars-of-their-own-charms?p=991284#post991284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and 2) There's no such thing as 'justification for moralization' in any sort of 'word from on high' in Exalted. If you feel people doing something is wrong by all means correct them, moralize at them, teach them what you believe to be right, but there's no Yahweh saying Thou Shalt Worship None But I that makes anything vaguely cult-like flat-out Bad-Wrong, for the particular example.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't true. There are plenty of beings of immense power handing down diktats from on high in Exalted that are used as a justification for various moral codes. The Unconquered Sun does that! So does Malfeas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Things might have bad intentions, like a cult that tortures people into following its' strictures, or bad outcomes, like a cult going mad, drinking koolaid, and mass-suiciding because of some twisted belief structure, but there's no D&amp;D-style &quot;capital-E reads to Divine Alignment spells as Evil&quot; to it that is objectively true. </div> </div> </div>This is only true in D&amp;D in the sense that &quot;various powerful beings have decided that this particular set of behaviors has the label 'Evil' attached to it, and they enforce cosmological consequences for having that label attached to you so far as they are able to.&quot;<br /> <br /> That doesn't make the actions defined as Evil in that rubric objectively evil, though; it just makes the rubric objectively a thing that exists and is enforced. And it is entirely possible to upend that rubric; the beings enforcing it in most D&amp;D settings are 100% murderable. You can destroy them and enforce your own rubric or none at all if you wish.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T15:08:55-07:00","id":992044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>taichara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/991204-how-aware-are-solars-of-their-own-charms?p=991966#post991966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Consciously choosing to have one's character plan to judge and nitpick another player's character for having a Charm from a published book is a good way to be counter-productive to that second player's <i>enjoyment of the game</i>, worldbuilding be damned.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hmmm... Maybe calm down a bit and read the opening post? Whoever said anything about making characters to judge other characters?<br /> <br /> What has been said is that a player (not character) challenged the in-world depiction of the use of a certain Charm. While players (not characters) were discussing in-game depictions of Charm use. That is all. What I suggested is that this be discussed with civility, not hostile dismissiviness.<br /> <br /> World building is about the enjoyment of the table as a whole. If a particular player's enjoyment of the game is detrimental to the overall table experience it is going to be reigned in, in the tables I arbitrate.<br /> <br /> I think your position is unexamined and premature. You are probably in favor of the enjoyment you like, and against the enjoyment you dislike. So being the enjoyment hero is probably not the flag you wanna raise.<br /> <br /> There is no reason to make the questioning player be an asshole, from the little information we have. He might be, he might not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/991204-how-aware-are-solars-of-their-own-charms?p=991995#post991995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Jen, toyboy is the closest specific word I can think of that sort of implies a male mistress (... but it only applies when your fancy piece is a bit younger, so may be a bit out if you're thinking about sexy &quot;Uncles&quot; ).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2746_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2746\" data-vbnamecard=\"2746\">TGUEIROS</a>, if a Charm says in the Charm it doesn't take conscious effect to apply and has forever changed his essence and such, I'd go with that. Otherwise I would be a bit leery about just deducing that from the rules. (Insert here standard Rules Are Not Physics and Charms Are Abstractions boilerplate we're all already bored of. We all know the drill.).<br /> <br /> Being permanent and having no cost could just be because the writers thought it wasn't worth making players track the cost of it or run out of essence for it, rather than because it literally isn't something that the character chooses to exert effort and control to do. Mind, you could certainly go either way if there's nothing specific.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that this should be a case by case arbitration. I just think that this specific Charm's description and effects allows such a depiction.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T16:13:59-07:00","id":992089,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/991204-how-aware-are-solars-of-their-own-charms?p=992029#post992029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't true. There are plenty of beings of immense power handing down diktats from on high in Exalted that are used as a justification for various moral codes. The Unconquered Sun does that! So does Malfeas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but both of them use very subjective terms while doing so. You get the UC commanding a reborn Solar to make the world &quot;righteous&quot;. You don't get them sitting down and the UC painstakingly mapping out; &quot;OK, murder is okay in X situation but not Y because...&quot;<br /> Exalts will interpret the Sun's words differently, but that's okay- they're <i>meant</i> to. That's why the power was given to so many different people in the first place. The UC <i>doesn't know</i> what changes should be made to Creation. He doesn't have some big game plan that incorporates Lyta killing children with Glimmering Horizon healing them. He only knows that his Chosen <i>can</i> end the Age of Sorrows, so he lets them decide how to do it. (Remember, the UC is one of the most pro-human, pro-freedom gods in the world. If he started revoking or bartering his favour to select Exalts, he'd be little better than the Primordials who enslaved him.) He can't be in 300 places at once, but they can. So he has to rely on their judgment instead of watching them all the time. He has no choice, and- well- it's not like things could get much worse.<br /> So the Solars get some justification for whatever they do, but no explicit orders to do anything.<br /> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":476,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","user":"Argonometra","date":". 10-27-2016, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T20:54:04-07:00","id":992224,"title":"","content":"Wow, that's a much bigger response than I was expecting, I'll have to pore over it all in greater detail, but I do want to weigh in breifly to confirm that it was a civil ooc discussion as TGUEIROS suggested. I felt compelled to throw this one out to the community because some of our players seemed uncomfortable with and/or confused by the new charm paradigm enough for it to harm future roleplaying between some of the PC's if not addressed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12339-liberty-king-gandalf","name":"Liberty King Gandalf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T04:38:00-07:00","id":992327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/991204-how-aware-are-solars-of-their-own-charms?p=992029#post992029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is only true in D&amp;D in the sense that &quot;various powerful beings have decided that this particular set of behaviors has the label 'Evil' attached to it, and they enforce cosmological consequences for having that label attached to you so far as they are able to.&quot;<br /> <br /> That doesn't make the actions defined as Evil in that rubric objectively evil, though; it just makes the rubric objectively a thing that exists and is enforced. And it is entirely possible to upend that rubric; the beings enforcing it in most D&amp;D settings are 100% murderable. You can destroy them and enforce your own rubric or none at all if you wish.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Dungeons and Dragons, morality is external and objective. Good, evil, law, and chaos make up the Outer planes the same way that fire, water, and earth make up the Inner planes. It's an actual metaphysical substance or energy.<br /> <br /> The gods do not define or control it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T05:56:01-07:00","id":992343,"title":"","content":"While I really liek the developer's idea about what charms are and how they function based on the text, there are certain charms that fly in teh face of that. I'm not sure how shooting a golden beam out of my sword is an extension of my excellence or how willing magnificent golden armor to protect me fits that bill either. It just struck me as odd and not in keeping with the philosophy of new game. My Dawn Caste however loves those melee charms. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1580-andrewm9","name":"andrewm9","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T07:52:51-07:00","id":992384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>andrewm9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/991204-how-aware-are-solars-of-their-own-charms?p=992343#post992343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I really liek the developer's idea about what charms are and how they function based on the text, there are certain charms that fly in teh face of that. I'm not sure how shooting a golden beam out of my sword is an extension of my excellence or how willing magnificent golden armor to protect me fits that bill either. It just struck me as odd and not in keeping with the philosophy of new game. My Dawn Caste however loves those melee charms. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't make sense because it was a retcon for 3e. The charms you refer too were 1e/2e charms that were so beloved they made the transition.<br /> <br /> In 1e and 2e, Exalted did speak about charms as discrete techniques. They even reference them in chapter fictions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T08:29:23-07:00","id":992392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/991204-how-aware-are-solars-of-their-own-charms?p=992327#post992327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In Dungeons and Dragons, morality is external and objective. Good, evil, law, and chaos make up the Outer planes the same way that fire, water, and earth make up the Inner planes. It's an actual metaphysical substance or energy.<br /> <br /> The gods do not define or control it.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, this is only true sometimes, in some D&amp;D settings. The gods (and various non-god beings) often do exercise extensive power over defining and controlling those energies.<br /> <br /> Second of all, even if I grant your point, I don't see how it undercuts my point at all. Good, evil, law, and chaos are simply labels that have been attached to those energies and the sorts of behavior and actions they reinforce-slash-are opposed to. That doesn't actually prove, in an objective sense, that what &quot;Good&quot; is promoting is morally correct and desireable; it only proves there's a set of energies and behaviors that have that label attached to them.<br /> <br /> And finally, those substances and energies are eminently able to be fucked with, redefined, and controlled by players. At the high end of D&amp;D play your characters become capable of doing things like walking into the Nine Hells, slapping Asmodeus right off his throne, and then imploding the entire place if they so desire.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T08:37:29-07:00","id":992395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/991204-how-aware-are-solars-of-their-own-charms?p=991995#post991995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Jen, toyboy is the closest specific word I can think of that sort of implies a male mistress (... but it only applies when your fancy piece is a bit younger, so may be a bit out if you're thinking about sexy &quot;Uncles&quot; ).</div> </div> </div> </div>The word you're looking for is &quot;boytoy.&quot; A toyboy would be something else entirely.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T08:44:43-07:00","id":992396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>andrewm9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/991204-how-aware-are-solars-of-their-own-charms?p=992343#post992343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I really liek the developer's idea about what charms are and how they function based on the text, there are certain charms that fly in teh face of that. I'm not sure how shooting a golden beam out of my sword is an extension of my excellence or how willing magnificent golden armor to protect me fits that bill either. It just struck me as odd and not in keeping with the philosophy of new game. My Dawn Caste however loves those melee charms. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think you have to caveat it a bit that Charms are built on mastery of essence as well as the skill (&quot;Charms are more of a holistic mixture of personal prowess and the harnessing of Essence than a group of discrete techniques or \u201cpowers.\u201d), so that's where those flashy, glowy Charms are coming from. Like if the character has learned how to fire beams from his sword its more like he just understands how to pull together essence in a way that forms a beam, and not so much he has learned a single technique really. (Though I think this stuff can get to be a bit of a potayto potahto discussion.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T09:30:04-07:00","id":992417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/991204-how-aware-are-solars-of-their-own-charms?p=992395#post992395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The word you're looking for is &quot;boytoy.&quot; A toyboy would be something else entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looks right to me. What do you take toyboy to mean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/651-throne","name":"Throne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T09:38:07-07:00","id":992419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/991204-how-aware-are-solars-of-their-own-charms?p=992417#post992417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Looks right to me. What do you take toyboy to mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>An action figure.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T15:26:57-07:00","id":992587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/991204-how-aware-are-solars-of-their-own-charms?p=992029#post992029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't true. There are plenty of beings of immense power handing down diktats from on high in Exalted that are used as a justification for various moral codes. The Unconquered Sun does that! So does Malfeas.</div> </div> </div> </div>The distinction I make here is that those beings are not omnipotent [only exceedingly powerful], not omniscient, and not considered infallible. Yes, a god might give a dictate, but I don't accumulate &quot;evil points&quot; for rejecting that dictate that eventually &quot;forces me to change my alignment&quot;. I don't have an alignment per se, and no amount of being good to the poor and downtrodden or, contrarily, murdering orphans to bathe in their blood has metaphysical ramifications such as 'you are now more vulnerable to specific classes of magical power', ala being Evil alignment and suffering extra effects from a Holy Word spell or whatever.<br /> <br /> Now, there are probably ramifications of other sorts, such as people objecting to my murdering of orphans and aiming to stop me by force, but this is not the impact of an Omniscient Alignment, this is the work of a mortal will taking umbrage at my actions and attempting to stop them.<br /> <br /> The important thing relevant to this is that there's nothing <i>inherently </i>wrong with fostering a cult; a given person may find it offensive that another is worshipped for their deeds and receives power as a result, but that is entirely that given person's opinion, not a reflection of some universal principle. Which is a lot of words to say &quot;Is the conflict you're brewing really that important, and maybe it would have been good to present your character's opinion on cult worship before the game started rather than springing it now and causing trouble?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T15:38:15-07:00","id":992592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/991204-how-aware-are-solars-of-their-own-charms?p=992587#post992587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The distinction I make here is that those beings are not omnipotent [only exceedingly powerful], not omniscient, and not considered infallible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a lot of RPG settings have beings of that nature. And when they do they're often not relevant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't have an alignment per se, and no amount of being good to the poor and downtrodden or, contrarily, murdering orphans to bathe in their blood has metaphysical ramifications such as 'you are now more vulnerable to specific classes of magical power', ala being Evil alignment and suffering extra effects from a Holy Word spell or whatever. </div> </div> </div>Worth noting that in both previous editions this wasn't entirely true; you could do things or undergo state changes that would get your classed as a Creature of Darkness, which did in fact render you increasingly vulnerable to certain kinds of magic. And that this effect operated omnisciently.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T16:16:43-07:00","id":992611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/991204-how-aware-are-solars-of-their-own-charms?p=992592#post992592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Worth noting that in both previous editions this wasn't entirely true; you could do things or undergo state changes that would get your classed as a Creature of Darkness, which did in fact render you increasingly vulnerable to certain kinds of magic. And that this effect operated omnisciently.</div> </div> </div> </div>Creature of Darkness isn't really much like alignment though. Your alignment in D&amp;D is determined by your actions. If you do evil things you get an evil alignment. If you do good things you get a good alignment. <br /> <br /> The Creature of Darkness tag is something you get slapped with regardless of your actions. For example, all ghosts are Creatures of Darkness, even if they're really nice and generous ghosts. Sure it's theoretically possible that some nice ghost might be able to get the Unconquered Sun to make an exception for her if she somehow gets his attention, but it's safe to say most nice ghosts get stuck as Creatures of Darkness. Same with demons and most other &quot;Creatures of Darkness.&quot; The specific actions don't matter, all that matters is that they were born (or became) a member of a type of race the Unconquered Sun hates.<br /> <br /> So to continue the D&amp;D comparison, the Creature of Darkness tag would be a bit more similar to a racial tag in D&amp;D than an alignment tag. Imagine a god in D&amp;D who grants his followers Bane Blessing that let them deal +2d6 damage vs goblinoids. The tag is determined by <i>what you are</i> rather than <i>what you do</i> - if you're born as a goblin, you're going to get smote, regardless of whether you are a good or evil goblin. Yes, there might be certain actions you can perform to overcome this such as using a permanent polymorph spell or reincarnating into something that isn't a goblin, but for the most part your own actions have no baring on whether you are considered a goblin (or Creature of Darkness in Exalted).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T03:01:26-07:00","id":992866,"title":"","content":"The D&amp;D contrast holds for people, but alignment is both descriptive amd proscriptive, as far as actions go. There are races of creature that are &quot;born evil&quot; (things like demons, many types of undead, etc.), and a particular individual *not* being evil is on the order of an Exalted demon not being a creature of darkness.<br /> <br /> So I guess what I mean is that the difference between the two concepts is that a non-naturally evil character can &quot;opt in&quot; to being evil with their actions, but a non-naturally CoD can't. A naturally CoD character definitely needs magical assistance to &quot;opt out&quot;; there are gradations of difficulty for the naturally-evil character doing the same, but it seems like as often as not such outliers are the result of freak mutation at their creation rather than any change the character precipitated by their own actions, which interestingly with CoDs happens the other direction (e.g. Five Days Darkness being born a CoD even though he's a god).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 10-25-2016, 06:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T06:56:48-07:00","id":992928,"title":"","content":"In D&amp;D, demons are evil by definition. A demon who managed to become non-evil would become something else, something not a demon. Orcs, on the other side, have a natural tendency toward evil, enough that assuming an orc raised by orcs is evil is not racism, just sensible, but an orc can be good and still be an orc. The same applies to elves in regards to good. Bust in Exalted, Good and Evil are not fundamental forces of the universe. However, they're still real things. Sell drugs you know are toxic? Evil. Tend the sick and injured, even if your motives are entirely mercenary? Good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T07:53:09-07:00","id":992945,"title":"","content":"Off topic, but I like to point out the absurdity of D+D style alignment with the following thought experiment :<br /> <br /> Two people are in a room with you. You must choose one to be pushed into an incinerator.<br /> <br /> You are not given the option of not choosing. Your Gods are watching and judging you. This is the most important event in your reality. Armageddon.<br /> <br /> One of these two people is the most virtuous and noble individual who has ever existed. The other is basically Hitler and Satan's baby.<br /> <br /> You do not get to know which is which... who do you choose?<br /> <br /> After this choice, how is your alignment changed?<br /> <br /> Now, the thing to understand about why D+D alignment is absurd is... every single situation in the real world is more or less like that. 'Good' and 'Evil' are not at all clearcut, often matters of interpretation and perspective, and hopelessly intermingled in an endless web of context that's sorta impossible to see more than a few layers into.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T08:41:22-07:00","id":992963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>andrewm9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/991204-how-aware-are-solars-of-their-own-charms?p=992343#post992343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I really liek the developer's idea about what charms are and how they function based on the text, there are certain charms that fly in teh face of that. I'm not sure how shooting a golden beam out of my sword is an extension of my excellence or how willing magnificent golden armor to protect me fits that bill either. It just struck me as odd and not in keeping with the philosophy of new game. My Dawn Caste however loves those melee charms. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Solar Exaltation doesn't grant discrete, X-Men-style superpowers, it just toggles your personal physics setting from &quot;Default&quot; to &quot;Anime&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T08:57:59-07:00","id":992970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/991204-how-aware-are-solars-of-their-own-charms?p=992945#post992945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Off topic, but I like to point out the absurdity of D+D style alignment with the following thought experiment :<br /> <br /> Two people are in a room with you. You must choose one to be pushed into an incinerator.<br /> <br /> You are not given the option of not choosing. Your Gods are watching and judging you. This is the most important event in your reality. Armageddon.<br /> <br /> One of these two people is the most virtuous and noble individual who has ever existed. The other is basically Hitler and Satan's baby.<br /> <br /> You do not get to know which is which... who do you choose?<br /> <br /> After this choice, how is your alignment changed?</div> </div> </div> </div>In regards to the problem, if you *must* choose one then you've been placed under a charm or geas, which means that your choice won't affect your alignment as you're not responsible for your actions.<br /> <br /> How you react to the situation itself might matter. If you toss someone into the incinerator while cackling in joy, yeah, you're probably swinging more evilish. If you attempt to fight the compulsion to murder them, that might be more good. If you're doing this out of a sense of duty, lawful.<br /> <br /> Of course, alignment is rarely defined by a single event.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, the thing to understand about why D+D alignment is absurd is... every single situation in the real world is more or less like that. 'Good' and 'Evil' are not at all clearcut, often matters of interpretation and perspective, and hopelessly intermingled in an endless web of context that's sorta impossible to see more than a few layers into. </div> </div> </div>Dungeons and Dragons alignment is interested in mirroring real world ethics about as much as Exalted is attempting to mirror real world physics.<br /> <br /> It's only 'absurd' if you think RPGs should be realistic. As Exalted is a game where I can literally punch someone so hard they land on the moon, its players should probably not look down on the absurdity of other games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 10-25-2016, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T09:44:27-07:00","id":992986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/991204-how-aware-are-solars-of-their-own-charms?p=992970#post992970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<br /> <br /> Dungeons and Dragons alignment is interested in mirroring real world ethics about as much as Exalted is attempting to mirror real world physics.<br /> <br /> It's only 'absurd' if you think RPGs should be realistic. As Exalted is a game where I can literally punch someone so hard they land on the moon, its players should probably not look down on the absurdity of other games.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is solid advice. DnD tarring and feathering is very gauche.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T09:52:16-07:00","id":992990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/991204-how-aware-are-solars-of-their-own-charms?p=992970#post992970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dungeons and Dragons alignment is interested in mirroring real world ethics about as much as Exalted is attempting to mirror real world physics.</div> </div> </div> </div>It claims not to be interested in such, then spends an eyebrow-raising amount of pagecount and rules text on it anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T10:33:29-07:00","id":993010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/991204-how-aware-are-solars-of-their-own-charms?p=992970#post992970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In regards to the problem, if you *must* choose one then you've been placed under a charm or geas, which means that your choice won't affect your alignment as you're not responsible for your actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, right here. If your character is under an effect which forces him to take an action and he has no choice in the matter, his alignment is not altered. If you were to cast Dominate Person on a Paladin and force the Paladin to commit an evil act, while the Paladin would likely feel absolutely horrible about what happened and feel a sense of responsibility for falling to the evil wizard's magical spell, the Paladin's alignment would not chance and he would not lose his status as a Paladin.<br /> <br /> I tend to find that most of the complains about D&amp;D's alignment system tend to come from people who don't have a solid understanding of how D&amp;D's alignment mechanics work. Kind of like THAC0, now that I think about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T19:10:54-07:00","id":993244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/991204-how-aware-are-solars-of-their-own-charms?p=992990#post992990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It claims not to be interested in such, then spends an eyebrow-raising amount of pagecount and rules text on it anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>Solely to <i>refute </i>those who read D&amp;D with the preconception that it is attempting to mirror real-world ethics or biology. If part of your audience has a fundamental misunderstanding about D&amp;D's goal*, then it is an author's responsibility to address that misunderstanding- even at the risk of going off-topic. For example, I don't proofread my writing because I want to, I do it so any future readers will understand what I was trying to say.<br /> <br /> * hint: to be a game, not the next <i>Mein Kampf</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T22:13:17-07:00","id":993319,"title":"","content":"A large amount of word count goes into what Good and Evil mean in the D&amp;D cosmology precisely because they do not entirely, match with our concepts of good and evil. For example, we consider the killing of intelligent beings to be no better than non-evil, and that only in very restricted circumstances, but in D&amp;D, it's clear that killing evil-aligned beings is not an evil act. How can we possibly know that? We can know it because paladins exist. If killing intelligent beings, regardless of their alignment, were inherently evil, paladins could not exist. But they do, so clearly it not an evil act to kill evil intelligent beings. That's the part a lot of people refuse to accept: in the default D&amp;D cosmology, Good and Evil do have objective meanings. They're not perspective based. A man who detonates the equivalent of a suicide bomb in the middle of a good-aligned village is not a holy warrior striking a brave blow against the evil enemies of his righteous faith. He's a mass murderer who has committed an act of evil. Period. End of sentence. The people who conceive the plan are evil, the people who assist him in executing it are evil. Period. End of sentence. At the best, they are of Neutral alignment and sliding fast toward Evil. A good-aligned person would not do such thing. Good and Evil in D&amp;D <i>mean things</i>. A person who does good things is a Good person, or at least heading that way, and contrariwise for evil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T23:15:57-07:00","id":993341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/991204-how-aware-are-solars-of-their-own-charms?p=993319#post993319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the part a lot of people refuse to accept: in the default D&amp;D cosmology, Good and Evil do have objective meanings. They're not perspective based.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. D&amp;D's setting isn't &quot;reality with necromancy and drow tacked on&quot;, it's an original world whose humans are called so because they <i>resemble</i> us physically- not because they are us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T15:31:16-07:00","id":993738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/991204-how-aware-are-solars-of-their-own-charms?p=993319#post993319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A large amount of word count goes into what Good and Evil mean in the D&amp;D cosmology precisely because they do not entirely, match with our concepts of good and evil. For example, we consider the killing of intelligent beings to be no better than non-evil, and that only in very restricted circumstances, but in D&amp;D, it's clear that killing evil-aligned beings is not an evil act. How can we possibly know that? We can know it because paladins exist. If killing intelligent beings, regardless of their alignment, were inherently evil, paladins could not exist. But they do, so clearly it not an evil act to kill evil intelligent beings. That's the part a lot of people refuse to accept: in the default D&amp;D cosmology, Good and Evil do have objective meanings. They're not perspective based. A man who detonates the equivalent of a suicide bomb in the middle of a good-aligned village is not a holy warrior striking a brave blow against the evil enemies of his righteous faith. He's a mass murderer who has committed an act of evil. Period. End of sentence. The people who conceive the plan are evil, the people who assist him in executing it are evil. Period. End of sentence. At the best, they are of Neutral alignment and sliding fast toward Evil. A good-aligned person would not do such thing. Good and Evil in D&amp;D <i>mean things</i>. A person who does good things is a Good person, or at least heading that way, and contrariwise for evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though this is true, it's worth noting that D&amp;D settings differ somewhat in how this gets expressed. Eberron, for example, tries to be a bit more grit and shades-of-grey, and so people tend toward neutrality, which makes the five-way World War that underlies the setting decouple right/wrong (subjective) from good/evil (objective). Contrast with Forgotten Realms, where when good-aligned nations go to war it's almost always to defend themselves from evil-aligned aggressors. The Oriental Adventures settings (Kara-Tur and later Rokugan) emphasize the Law/Chaos dynamic over the Good/Evil one, but both do of course still exist. Planescape embraces and doubles down on the whole alignment thing because it's mostly set in the Outer Planes where these cosmic concepts find their purest expression.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 10-26-2016, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T21:59:44-07:00","id":993885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/991204-how-aware-are-solars-of-their-own-charms?p=993319#post993319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the part a lot of people refuse to accept: in the default D&amp;D cosmology, Good and Evil do have objective meanings.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they don't. At least, not in the usual understanding of good and evil.<br /> <br /> There are forces in the D&amp;D cosmology that have assembled a variety of acts and behaviors and labelled them under the rubric of &quot;good&quot; and another set of acts and behaviors they have labelled under the rubric of &quot;evil.&quot; Also rubrics exist for law and chaos. These rubrics enforce certain consequences for your actions.<br /> <br /> And that's it. They do not prove, in any objective way, that those acts and behaviors actually <i>are</i> 'good' or 'evil.' The rubric exists. The consequences it provides exist. The labels that are attached to it exists. Those are objective, provable fact.<br /> <br /> Anything above and beyond that is not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T03:57:10-07:00","id":993970,"title":"","content":"Not by default, no. The only forces to have come down from on high with a mandate to enforce what makes Good good and Evil evil are the authors, and while they've done a pretty shitty job of it, there's nothing indicating that, &quot;like, murder is only Evil because THE GODS say it is! But who's saying THE GODS have the right of it?&quot; <br /> <br /> I'll admit, I'm not intimately familiar with every edition, but no Alignment section in any PHB I've read has ever expressed alignment as something the gods decide on or can actively manipulate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T10:14:55-07:00","id":994092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/991204-how-aware-are-solars-of-their-own-charms?p=993885#post993885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, they don't. At least, not in the usual understanding of good and evil.<br /> <br /> There are forces in the D&amp;D cosmology that have assembled a variety of acts and behaviors and labelled them under the rubric of &quot;good&quot; and another set of acts and behaviors they have labelled under the rubric of &quot;evil.&quot; Also rubrics exist for law and chaos. These rubrics enforce certain consequences for your actions.<br /> <br /> And that's it. They do not prove, in any objective way, that those acts and behaviors actually <i>are</i> 'good' or 'evil.' The rubric exists. The consequences it provides exist. The labels that are attached to it exists. Those are objective, provable fact.<br /> <br /> Anything above and beyond that is not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm not sure what you're referring to by &quot;forces&quot;. The Good/Evil axis and the Law/Chaos axis are consistently on a level with Shinma in terms of cosmic primacy, even transcending universes (unless you assume Crystal Spheres in which case there's really just one universe, I suppose). Using Detect Evil to tell you something is &quot;Evil&quot; isn't, so far as any D&amp;D setting I've ever read would characterize it, all that different from using depth perception to tell you something is &quot;far away&quot;. There are certainly no intelligences empowered to define or change the &quot;rubric&quot;, as you say, anywhere that I've ever seen.<br /> <br /> Further, even taking your statement at face value, between the rubric, the consequences, and the labels, I'm not sure what part of alignment is left to be subjective? Unless you're just making a distinction between capital-G &quot;Good&quot;, as in the cosmic principle, and little-g &quot;good&quot;, the subjective type of morality we have in real life? I.e, someone can still be doing 'good' from a subjective, in-setting personal and/or cultural perspective but be committing 'Evil' in the objective eyes of the fictional universe they live in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 10-27-2016, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}